; The by-design nested-sugar shape: a *plain-data* parent `(plain …)` with NO
; `:lowering`, holding a lowerable `(inner)`. The container consumes the child
; as data; the child lowers on its own. Because the parent is not lowerable, the
; nested-lowerable lint never fires — this is the supported pattern, the
; negative-space regression guard at the pipeline level. The only emitted form
; is `inner-normal`, an `:open` terminal, so the whole document is clean.
(plugin :name nestclean :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name plain :open true)
  (form :name inner :open true
    :lowering (lowering :hook test/identity-v1 :produces [inner-normal]))

  ; Identity-hook terminal.
  (form :name inner-normal :open true))

(plain (inner))
